  "details": "SDK Version: 3.10.4\n\nIn FilterAnimatorEvents() (UnityEventFilter.cs:402), when an Animator with no runtimeAnimatorController is encountered, the code executes 'return' instead of 'continue'. This exits the entire foreach loop, leaving all subsequent Animators in the hierarchy unchecked and their AnimationEvents unsanitized.\n\nRepro steps:\n\n1. Create a world project (SDK 3.10.4)\n\n2. Create a parent GameObject \"TestParent\"\n\n3. Under TestParent: add \"A_EmptyAnimator\" (Animator, no controller) above \"B_ForbiddenEvent\" (Animator with a clip containing a non-allowed AnimationEvent)\n\n4. Call UnityEventFilter.FilterEvents(testParent) in Play mode\n\nExpected: [UnityEventFilter] Removed AnimationEvents log appears — B's event is sanitized\n\nActual: No removal log. The forbidden AnimationEvent fires.\n\nProof — only the order matters:\n\n- A above B: ForbiddenFunction executes (screenshot 1)\n\n- B above A: [UnityEventFilter] Removed AnimationEvents from 'B_ForbiddenEvent' (screenshot 2)\n\nFix: Line 402, change 'return' to 'continue'",
